===== cellwork_send =====
Any cell seat: send one durable cell message to `captain`, a member of this cell by name, or `<cellId>/<captain|member>` for a cell in this cell's tree (a sub-cell it registered, or its parent). Optional STRUCTURED mail: `kind` (`message`|`question`|`answer`); a question carries `options` (+`multiSelect`) and its `questionId` defaults to its own message id; an answer carries `replyTo` (the question's message id), `selected` (the offered labels copied VERBATIM) and/or `custom` — an unknown label is refused WITH the valid label list, and the answer's `questionId` defaults to the answered question's. `broadcast:true` mints ONE ROW PER SEAT of the target cell (the sender excluded). MAILBOX FULL: a recipient with `mail.maxUndelivered` undelivered messages is refused (the key is read per call from the workspace config; its DEFAULT is 8, and `agent_teams_mail` shares the SAME bound, so the official tool is not a fallback). Two recoveries: acknowledge that inbox (`cellwork_inbox` for a cell seat, or `agent_teams_mail {action:"read"}` for a team member), or reassign the rows behind it (`cellwork_dispatch {reassign:[{task_id, owner}]}`). The row(s) are written to the workspace mailbox FIRST (atomic fan-out through the shared store), then a wake-up is attempted per row when the sender is this cell's captain and the recipient holds a handle; the attempt's outcome is appended as a `wake` record, so a failed wake-up leaves the row in place and is surfaced on `cellwork_supervise`. The journal carries the `cell:<cellId>` stamp.

